Photoplasm follows a Pioreactor-style open-source model: core software is released under the MIT License, which permits broad reuse with required copyright and license attribution; documentation is licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0; and hardware designs are licensed under CERN-OHL-S v2, both of which preserve attribution and reciprocal licensing requirements. The Photoplasm name, branding, proprietary know-how, unpublished processes, and separately protected inventions remain outside those blanket licenses.



